'''''Tamarix africana''''', also known as the '''African tamarisk''', is a species of tree in the family [[Tamaricaceae]]. They have a self-supporting growth form and simple leaves. Individuals can grow to 6.3 m.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Tamarix africana Poir. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/585673|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Tamarix africana (African Tamarisk) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/TAMR/Tamarix_africana.php |access-date=2022-03-07 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref>

